WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.752 --> 00:00:07.210
SPEAKER: Give me
a minute, and I'll

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.880
show you how Cloud Storage
can help you store objects

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.580
while optimizing the
performance of your apps.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.340
Google Cloud Storage is a
global, secure, and scalable

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.500
object or blob store for
mutable, unstructured data,

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.627
such as images,
videos, and documents.

00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:22.210
When you're building
an app, you store

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.600
objects in buckets, which are
associated with a project.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.300
You can then upload objects to
the bucket and download objects

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.930
from it using the console
or gsutil commands.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:33.623
By default, data at
rest is encrypted,

00:00:33.623 --> 00:00:36.040
and you have options to secure
it with your own encryption

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.060
keys.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.150
You can grant permission to
specific members in teams

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.970
or make the objects fully
public for mobile and web

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:44.200
applications.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.300
When creating buckets,
you have options

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.580
depending on budget,
availability, and access

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:49.780
frequency.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.940
Choose Standard Regional
or Multi-regional buckets

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.800
for high performance,
frequent access,

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.050
and highest
availability, Nearline

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.090
for once-a-month
access, Coldline

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.490
for less than once a
quarter, and Archive for data

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:02.680
that you want to
put away for years.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.510
The objects are
automatically versioned.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:06.280
And with Object
Lifecycle Management,

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.310
you can automatically transition
the data to lower cost storage

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:11.230
classes when it
reaches a certain age

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:13.910
or when you store a newer
version of the file.

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:15.730
Once you have stored
the data, accessing it

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:19.690
is easy with a single API call
for all the storage classes.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.750
Cloud Storage is optimal to use
for hosting static websites,

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.650
streaming, and
storing documents.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.620
It's widely used for
backups and archives.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.850
And it is a great data-like
choice for Big Data and ML.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.350
Next time you are thinking about
storing data, take a minute

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:33.670
and look at cloud storage.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:37.560
For more info, check out
Cloud.google.com/storage.

